<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-ITALY'S COMPAGNONI WINS GIANT SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ITALY'S COMPAGNONI WINS GIANT SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>CORTINA D'AMPEZZO, Italy 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Deborah Compagnoni won a women's Alpine skiing World Cup giant slalom on Sunday, according to provisional results.</p>
<p>Compagnoni clocked a combined time of two minutes 38.25 seconds.</p>
<p>Germany's Katja Seizinger was second in 2:38.84 and Switzerland's Sonja Nef third in 2:39.67.</p>
